course: dictionary
lesson: 6687
title: Blocking the way
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To obstruct something means to block it so that things cannot get past. It is a verb, so you can say obstruct, obstructs, obstructed or obstructing. The clerk tells a passenger, «you're obstructing the other passengers», which means you are standing in the way so they cannot get past.
explain: Obstruct can be used for many things. A parked van can obstruct a road, a broken pipe can be obstructed, and a tall bush can obstruct the view. You can also obstruct a plan or try to stop something happening, as in obstruct the police.
explain: The clues help you find the meaning. The other passengers need to get past, and you are in their way. Swap in blocking: «you're blocking the other passengers» still makes sense, so obstructing means blocking.
fact: Obstruct means to block something so that things cannot pass.
fact: «You're obstructing the other passengers» means you are blocking them.
fact: In sport, obstructing means blocking another player unfairly, and the referee can give a foul for it.
fact: Never obstruct a fire exit or an ambulance, because people and help need to get through.
fact: A tree can obstruct the view when it stands in front of a window or a road sign.
exercise: «You're obstructing the other passengers.» What does obstructing mean here? | Thanking | *Blocking | Helping | Singing to
exercise: Safety sign: Never obstruct a fire exit. What must you never do to a fire exit? | *Block it so people cannot get out | Count its steps | Paint it | Decorate it with flowers
exercise: In a football match, a player is given a foul for obstructing an opponent. What has the player done? | Cheered for the other team | Walked the ball out of play | *Blocked another player unfairly | Scored a goal
test: A tree that grows in front of a window can obstruct the what? | Floor | *View | Sky | Door
test: A blocked pipe is obstructed, so water cannot flow. What does obstructed mean for a pipe? | Made bigger | Painted red | Flowing freely | *Blocked so nothing can pass
exam: Which word means the same as obstruct in «you're obstructing the other passengers»? | Thanking | Following | *Blocking | Helping
